    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Revamped the entire approach by changing the event order. The \"root cause\" is that successful `BufReadCmd` reads skip `FileType` used after normal `BufReadPost`.\r\n\r\nThis means reload could clear syntax state without rerunning filetype setup (basically the issue I described before but applied to the event order).\r\n\r\nIf this is not what you're looking for I can only imagine doing a dirvish-style \"re-set filetype=directory after `nvim.dir` reloads\" approach",
            "created_at": "2026-07-10T23:20:17Z",
